<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
   <title>2.3.5: Practice</title>
   <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
      <md:content-id>m00413</md:content-id>
      <md:title>2.3.5: Practice</md:title>
      <md:uuid>6207154b-b57a-476c-ae69-38e85a079e24</md:uuid>
   </metadata>
   <content>
      <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">
         <para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this
            lesson.</para>

            <exercise id="d6f8070d-51ee-4e35-9188-c3c9a9779198" class="multiple-choice">
               <problem id="prob-00001">
                  <para id="para-00002">Lin is solving this system of equations:</para>
                  <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">{</m:mo><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>34</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable></m:mrow></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00004">She starts by rearranging the second equation to isolate the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> variable:
                     <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1.5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. She then substitutes the expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1.5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> in the first equation, as shown:</para>
                  <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1.5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>34</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>7.5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>34</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1.5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>54</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>36</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1.5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1.5</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>36</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>58</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00010">Does Lin’s solution of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>36</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>58</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> makes both equations in the system
                     true?</para>
                  <para id="para-00011">Multiple Choice:</para>
                  <para id="para-00012">yes; Her solution makes both equations true.</para>
                  <para id="para-00013">No; Her solution does not make both equations true.</para>
               </problem>
               <solution id="sol-00001">
                  <para id="para-00014">Correct! No; Her solution does not make both equations true.</para>
                  <para id="para-00015">Try again. Revisit activity 2.3.2.</para>
                  <para id="para-00016">The correct answer is that Lin’s solution does not make both equations true.</para>
               </solution>
            </exercise>

            <exercise id="fc2e0fa3-9cd1-4dff-987c-17aa1afa8afd" class="multiple-choice">
               <problem id="prob-00002">
                  <para id="para-00017">Which of the following is true of Lin’s solution?</para>
                  <para id="para-00018">Multiple Choice:</para>
                  <para id="para-00019">Lin made a multiplication error. The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>.</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
                  <para id="para-00020">Lin made a multiplication error. The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, or (9,4).</para>
                  <para id="para-00021">Lin made an addition error. The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>,
                     or (0,4).</para>
                  <para id="para-00022">Lin’s solution of (-36, 58) is correct.</para>
               </problem>
               <solution id="sol-00002">
                  <para id="para-00023">Correct! Lin made a multiplication error. The correct answer is x = 4 and y
                     = -2, or (4,-2).</para>
                  <para id="para-00024">Try again. Revisit activity 2.3.2.</para>
                  <para id="para-00025">The correct answer is Lin made a multiplication error. The correct answer is
                     <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
               </solution>
            </exercise>

         <para id="para-00026">In 3 - 9, solve the systems of equations by substitution.</para>
            <exercise id="a42eaa70-a2fc-4597-8102-6b37c1b48ad6" class="multiple-choice">
               <problem id="prob-00003">
                  <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">{</m:mo><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix"/></m:mrow></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00028">Multiple Choice:</para>
                  <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
               <solution id="sol-00003">
                  <para id="para-00033">Correct! (1,−4)</para>
                  <para id="para-00034">Try again. Revisit activities 2.3.3 and 2.3.4.</para>
                  <para id="para-00035">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
                  <para id="para-00036">Check the solution in both equations.</para>
                  <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>✓</m:mi></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mi>✓</m:mi></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00039">(4,-1) Makes both equations in the system true, therefore it is a solution.</para>
               </solution>
            </exercise>

            <exercise id="_527afbcf-da67-43bf-a980-73f4d3ab4824" class="multiple-choice">
               <problem id="prob-00004">
                  <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">{</m:mo><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix"/></m:mrow></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00041">Multiple Choice:</para>
                  <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
               <solution id="sol-00004">
                  <para id="para-00046">Correct! (−3,2)</para>
                  <para id="para-00047">Try again. Revisit activities 2.3.3 and 2.3.4.</para>
                  <para id="para-00048">The correct answer is (−3,2).</para>
                  <para id="para-00049">Check the solution in both equations.</para>
                  <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mi>−</m:mi></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mi>✓</m:mi></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>✓</m:mi></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00052">(-3,2) Makes both equations in the system true, therefore it is a solution.</para>
               </solution>
            </exercise>
            <exercise id="_6193e47f-ea4f-4dce-ad7b-26c2028856de" class="multiple-choice">
               <problem id="prob-00005">
                  <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">{</m:mo><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>14</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="postfix"/></m:mrow></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00054">Multiple Choice:</para>
                  <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
               <solution id="sol-00005">
                  <para id="para-00059">Correct! (1,4)</para>
                  <para id="para-00060">Try again. Revisit activities 2.3.3 and 2.3.4.</para>
                  <para id="para-00061">The correct answer is (1,4).</para>
                  <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>✓</m:mi></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>14</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>14</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>14</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mi>✓</m:mi></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00064">(1,4) Makes both equations in the system true, therefore it is a solution.</para>
               </solution>
